{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1001", "sample_idx": 37, "model_name": "mistralai/mistral-small-4-119b-2603", "content": "In sooth mine heart doth leap with joy to craft thy journey through fair Nippon’s realm. Behold thine itinerary writ in thy desired tongue.\n\n**Act I: The Rising Sun – Tokyo’s Grand Stage**\n\n**Scene I: Arrival in the City of Shoguns**\nUpon thy first footfall in Tokyo’s bustling lanes thou shalt be met by the neon glow of Shibuya’s crosswalk like stars fallen to earth. Seek thee the historic Asakusa quarter where the Senso-ji Temple doth stand proud and ancient. Pray at its gates and take in the scent of incense that doth waft through the air like whispers of the gods.\n\n**Scene II: The Imperial Playhouse**\nJourney to the Imperial Palace and its gardens where the chrysanthemum and the cherry blossom do vie for supremacy in nature’s grand design. Walk the outer grounds and marvel at the moat that doth encircle the palace like a dragon’s embrace.\n\n**Scene III: The Feast of a Thousand Flavors**\nWhen night doth fall thou shalt repair to the izakayas of Shinjuku where the sake flows like the river of time itself. Partake of yakitori and tempura whilst the sounds of shamisen and taiko drums fill thine ears like a symphony of old.\n\n**Act II: The Mountain’s Lament – Hakone’s Soothing Embrace**\n\n**Scene I: The Hot Springs’ Embrace**\nHie thee to Hakone where the steam of onsen doth rise like the sighs of spirits long passed. Sink thy weary bones into waters warmed by the earth’s own breath and let the cares of the world melt away as snow beneath the morning sun.\n\n**Scene II: The View from Mount Fuji’s Shoulder**\nUpon the morrow ascend the ropeway to Owakudani and gaze upon the steaming vents and sulfurous springs. Should fortune favor thee with clear skies thou mayst espy Mount Fuji standing tall and proud like a sentinel of old watching o’er the land.\n\n**Act III: The Ancient Capital – Kyoto’s Timeless Dance**\n\n**Scene I: Temples of Splendor and Stone**\nEnter Kyoto the heart of old Japan where the temples stand as sentinels of history. Marvel at Kinkaku-ji the Golden Pavilion that doth gleam like a jewel upon the earth. Wander through Fushimi Inari’s torii gates that march up the mountain like an army of vermilion clad soldiers.\n\n**Scene II: The Geisha’s Grace**\nWhen evening doth descend seek thee the Gion quarter where the geisha and maiko do glide like ghosts of a bygone age. Should fortune favor thee thou mayst espy one in passing and catch a glimpse of a world untouched by time.\n\n**Scene III: The Cherry Blossom’s Fleeting Kiss**\nIf thy journey be in spring thee must wander the Philosopher’s Path where the cherry blossoms do rain down like petals from heaven’s own garden. Sit beneath their fleeting beauty and ponder the transient nature of all things.\n\n**Act IV: The Culmination – Osaka’s Revelry**\n\n**Scene I: The Castle of the Rising Sun**\nJourney to Osaka and its mighty castle that doth stand as a testament to power and resilience. Walk its walls and gaze upon the city that doth sprawl beneath thee like a living tapestry.\n\n**Scene II: The Thieves’ Market and the Feast of the Gods**\nDescend to Dotonbori where the lights do dance upon the water and the takoyaki doth sizzle in the pan. Partake of okonomiyaki and let thy heart be merry as thou art surrounded by the joyous clamor of the people.\n\n**Epilogue: The Farewell**\n\nWhen the time comes to depart reflect upon thy journey through lands both ancient and new. Carry with thee the memories of temples and teahouses the bustle of cities and the tranquility of nature’s embrace. Fare thee well and may thy path be ever bright.", "logprobs": [{"token": "In", "logprob": -2.038621187210083}, {"token": " so", "logprob": -0.12756425142288208}, {"token": "oth", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " mine", "logprob": -1.3010929822921753}, {"token": " heart", "logprob": -2.4258077144622803}, {"token": " d", "logprob": -0.3182893395423889}, {"toke